it's good enough for the internet,

01:03:08.210 --> 01:03:11.030
'cause you're seeing it.
It's cool, it's cool.

01:03:11.030 --> 01:03:12.390
But then.
It's a much better camera.

01:03:12.390 --> 01:03:13.730
But the second thing.

01:03:13.730 --> 01:03:15.480
Yeah, 'cause the first one was
probably just a film camera.

01:03:15.480 --> 01:03:18.340
The second picture was
while we were walking.

01:03:18.340 --> 01:03:19.270
So, it's really easy,

01:03:19.270 --> 01:03:21.463
you just walk on the Golden Gate Bridge.

01:03:22.753 --> 01:03:26.330
And, this one was much easier
to sort of get the angle,

01:03:26.330 --> 01:03:27.670
and it was just two people.

01:03:27.670 --> 01:03:28.503
It was Locke in front of Jessie.

01:03:28.503 --> 01:03:30.050
Dang, look at that noggin.

01:03:30.050 --> 01:03:32.300
And it, and me taking the picture, so.

01:03:32.300 --> 01:03:34.090
Like Dr. Evil.

01:03:34.090 --> 01:03:36.340
Let's see, so again.

01:03:36.340 --> 01:03:40.000
This was not easy, and
there was some consternation

01:03:40.000 --> 01:03:41.690
from Locke in this one.

01:03:41.690 --> 01:03:42.523
Because I was like,

01:03:42.523 --> 01:03:43.620
"Dude, no, you gotta look mean,

01:03:43.620 --> 01:03:44.500
you gotta look madder."

01:03:44.500 --> 01:03:46.530
And like, this is as mad
as he was willing to-

01:03:46.530 --> 01:03:47.363
That's pretty good.

01:03:47.363 --> 01:03:48.196
To go, but no.

01:03:48.196 --> 01:03:49.410
You should have shaved his head for it.

01:03:49.410 --> 01:03:53.900
So, Jessie posted this one on her Twitter,

01:03:53.900 --> 01:03:55.590
it's got like, I don't know.

01:03:55.590 --> 01:03:57.590
It's got like 12,000 likes,
when I'm recording this.

01:03:57.590 --> 01:04:00.130
I'm sure it's got more than that now but,

01:04:00.130 --> 01:04:02.550
people were really into this

01:04:02.550 --> 01:04:05.850
and commented on the fact
that Jessie does not age.

01:04:05.850 --> 01:04:07.583
Which she, she really hasn't.

01:04:08.680 --> 01:04:10.310
Locke has, look at him boy.

01:04:10.310 --> 01:04:12.110
Yeah, he's changed quite a bit.

01:04:12.110 --> 01:04:14.830
He's still a little, got a lot of angst.

01:04:14.830 --> 01:04:16.660
Well, it seems like you made him do that.

01:04:16.660 --> 01:04:17.493
But you know, we had a...

01:04:17.493 --> 01:04:19.080
This guy, you know what, it was worth it.

01:04:19.080 --> 01:04:22.033
We had a really good moment
on the Golden Gate Bridge.

01:04:23.100 --> 01:04:24.950
Like I said, you know,

01:04:24.950 --> 01:04:27.190
there was a moment when
we were getting ready to,

01:04:27.190 --> 01:04:29.840
when we had just gotten
into the car to leave,

01:04:29.840 --> 01:04:30.673
where Shepherd was like,

01:04:30.673 --> 01:04:35.010
"Dad, couldn't you just let
Locke drive in his own car,

01:04:35.010 --> 01:04:36.533
and follow us up to San Francisco?"

01:04:36.533 --> 01:04:39.627
And I was like, "You guys
are so spoiled, man."

01:04:39.627 --> 01:04:40.927
"Like, the fact that you
would even ask that."

01:04:40.927 --> 01:04:42.560
"You what my dad would've said,

01:04:42.560 --> 01:04:46.180
if I had asked if one of us
could have driven separately?"

01:04:46.180 --> 01:04:48.610
I was like, "I'm not even
gonna answer that question".

01:04:48.610 --> 01:04:51.810
But, they weren't getting along, right.

01:04:51.810 --> 01:04:54.400
And this is probably
typical of a lot of families

01:04:54.400 --> 01:04:55.470
when you're getting ready to travel.

01:04:55.470 --> 01:04:56.340
It's like, that just seems,

01:04:56.340 --> 01:04:58.140
that's when everything goes wrong.

01:04:58.140 --> 01:04:59.810
That's when everybody starts getting mad,

01:04:59.810 --> 01:05:01.310
everybody's fuses get super short.

01:05:01.310 --> 01:05:02.920
Then y'all just get
into of the car together

01:05:02.920 --> 01:05:04.650
and go, right.

01:05:04.650 --> 01:05:06.940
And we did, everybody did calm down.

01:05:06.940 --> 01:05:10.590
But there were some times where there was

01:05:12.030 --> 01:05:15.120
some, Locke and Shepherd
will kind of fight each other

01:05:15.120 --> 01:05:16.340
a little bit, like playfully.

01:05:16.340 --> 01:05:18.490
And sometimes, it'll get a
little bit outta hand, you know.

01:05:18.490 --> 01:05:19.710
Two boys fighting,

01:05:19.710 --> 01:05:21.973
and then all of a sudden somebody's upset,

01:05:23.070 --> 01:05:25.332
and I kind of have to break it up.

01:05:25.332 --> 01:05:26.640
And of course,

01:05:26.640 --> 01:05:31.530
everyone has their own stuff
that they get upset about.

01:05:31.530 --> 01:05:34.570
But when we were walking
on the Golden Gate Bridge,

01:05:34.570 --> 01:05:36.490
I don't remember exactly what Locke said,

01:05:36.490 --> 01:05:37.967
but he essentially says something like,

01:05:37.967 --> 01:05:41.383
"Listen, we're all gonna die one day."

01:05:43.160 --> 01:05:45.650
He was like, and I, we were
also kind of, honestly,

01:05:45.650 --> 01:05:47.122
we were thinking about people-

01:05:47.122 --> 01:05:47.955
Jumping.

01:05:47.955 --> 01:05:49.630
Jumping off the bridge because it's like,

01:05:49.630 --> 01:05:52.290
Locke was like 1,700 people a year or,

01:05:52.290 --> 01:05:53.670
or 1700 people total.

01:05:53.670 --> 01:05:55.360
I can't, it's a lot of people.

01:05:55.360 --> 01:05:58.210
In fact, they're
installing a net right now,

01:05:58.210 --> 01:06:03.070
and the supports are out there
ready to receive the net.

01:06:03.070 --> 01:06:04.650
So, people won't jump off the bridge.

01:06:04.650 --> 01:06:07.010
But, once you get to the
middle of the bridge,

01:06:07.010 --> 01:06:08.840
there's nothing to keep
you from jumping off.

01:06:08.840 --> 01:06:11.830
Like there's no more fence and stuff.

01:06:11.830 --> 01:06:14.090
They have fence up so
that you can't get on the

01:06:14.090 --> 01:06:17.190
giant circular wire that goes to the top,

01:06:17.190 --> 01:06:19.290
'cause they don't want
you to like dare devils.

01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:20.917
But in the middle, they're like,

01:06:20.917 --> 01:06:21.750
"If people are gonna do this,

01:06:21.750 --> 01:06:22.630
they're gonna do this."

01:06:22.630 --> 01:06:24.200
Until now, that they're
installing the net.

01:06:24.200 --> 01:06:25.260
So, it was on the brain.

01:06:25.260 --> 01:06:29.270
So, it gives you this sense
of your own mortality.

01:06:29.270 --> 01:06:30.147
And he was just like,

01:06:30.147 --> 01:06:33.926
"Listen, we're all gonna die
one day and I love you guys."

01:06:33.926 --> 01:06:34.759
Ha.

01:06:34.759 --> 01:06:37.647
"And I'm sorry for when I'm a jerk."

01:06:39.180 --> 01:06:40.880
And it was like, this is beautiful.

01:06:40.880 --> 01:06:42.247
And we were all like, "We're sorry too."

01:06:42.247 --> 01:06:44.152
"Like we're all jerks sometimes."

01:06:44.152 --> 01:06:44.985
Huh.

01:06:44.985 --> 01:06:47.210
And just, I think he ended
up saying something like,

01:06:47.210 --> 01:06:48.710
and "I like what, you know,

01:06:48.710 --> 01:06:51.030
where I go to school
doesn't even really matter."

01:06:51.030 --> 01:06:51.863
Huh.

01:06:51.863 --> 01:06:53.077
And I was, I was kinda like,

01:06:53.077 --> 01:06:54.844
"Well, it kind of does, but no"

01:06:54.844 --> 01:06:56.520
but I didn't say anything at the time

01:06:56.520 --> 01:06:59.640
we had like a beautiful group hug.

01:06:59.640 --> 01:07:00.473
That's great.

01:07:00.473 --> 01:07:01.710
You know what I would've
said at that moment?

01:07:01.710 --> 01:07:03.450
I would've said, "You know what?

01:07:03.450 --> 01:07:04.317
This is beautiful."

01:07:04.317 --> 01:07:06.050
"Let's get a picture."

01:07:06.050 --> 01:07:08.650
And then I would've
thrown it back into chaos.

01:07:08.650 --> 01:07:09.970
Yeah, we didn't get a picture of that.

01:07:09.970 --> 01:07:12.560
You just got a group hug
on the Golden Gate Bridge?

01:07:12.560 --> 01:07:14.491
We did, we got a group hug
on the Golden Gate Bridge.

01:07:14.491 --> 01:07:15.324
Wow.

01:07:15.324 --> 01:07:17.280
We also had a really
interesting thing happen,

